(Technical Whitepaper: Model Fine-Tuning vs RAG Architecture) Tj T*
(Author: Enterprise Document Intelligence Group) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Executive Overview:) Tj T*
(Fine-tuning adjusts internal neural network weights, whereas RAG provides an external,) Tj T*
(dynamic non-parametric memory store without model retraining.) Tj T*
(For rapidly evolving enterprise documents, RAG is 20x more cost-effective than continuous fine-tuning.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 1: Data Freshness and Cost Analysis) Tj T*
(Fine-tuning costs approximately $450 to $1,800 per training run on specialized clusters.) Tj T*
(In contrast, vector ingestion with DocuMind costs less than $0.002 per document.) Tj T*
ET
